<task id="003" project="messaging-communication-app-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Schema: `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction (message grain) — 6 fields (communication lookup, systemuser, contact, role {From,To,Cc,Bcc}, addresstext, isresolved) + primary name</title>
    <phase>W0 — Schema + Foundation + ADR</phase>
    <status>completed</status>
    <estimated-hours>5</estimated-hours>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <blocks>050, 051</blocks>
    <tags>dataverse, schema</tags>
    <rigor>STANDARD</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Creates a NEW Dataverse entity (junction) — no BFF code, no Step 9.5 gates. STANDARD per §8 (new-surface schema creation with a locked field set). §11 Component Justification REQUIRED (a new entity is introduced; spec supplies the concrete cost-of-doing-nothing). The ADR-034 path-C tension is documented by the sibling ADR task (004), not decided here.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W0-B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-08</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Create the NEW `sprk_communicationparticipant` junction that makes participants QUERYABLE at message grain — the structure the `participant=` facet (FR-02) and external-party visibility depend on. Today participant data is unqueryable: `sprk_from`/`sprk_to`/`sprk_cc` are `;`-joined TEXT and no junction exists (`notes/r2-resource-investigation.md` §5). This task creates the table + its 6 locked fields ONLY — the capture/send-time WRITE is task 050, the `participant=` join is task 051.

    Create, via the `dataverse-create-schema` skill patterns, `sprk_communicationparticipant` with EXACTLY these fields (locked 2026-07-18, spec FR-08 — do NOT add, drop, or rename):

    1. **`sprk_communication`** — Lookup → `sprk_communication` (**required**; the message-grain parent, per owner Q-A: message grain only, no thread-grain rows).
    2. **`sprk_systemuser`** — Lookup → `systemuser` (nullable).
    3. **`sprk_contact`** — Lookup → `contact` (nullable). **Exactly one of `sprk_systemuser` / `sprk_contact` is set for a resolved person; BOTH null for an unresolved external address.** (Enforced by the write, task 050; schema allows both nullable.)
    4. **`sprk_role`** — Choice: `From` / `To` / `Cc` / `Bcc` (assign the integer values planned in task 001's audit note).
    5. **`sprk_addresstext`** — Text (raw email; populated for unresolved external parties and retained for resolved ones as provenance).
    6. **`sprk_isresolved`** — Boolean (false when no person lookup is set; enables back-fill when a `contact` is later created).
    7. **`sprk_name`** — primary Text (e.g. `"{personDisplay|address} — {role}"`).

    Two typed nullable person lookups (systemuser/contact), NOT the ADR-034 Guid+type tuple and NOT a polymorphic lookup — this is the owner-approved path-C comply-with-intent (Q-C; only 2 targets, so typed lookups honor ADR-034's intent while adding FK integrity + DataGrid person-chip auto-derivation). Verify the `sprk_role` integers via task 001's plan / MCP before assignment. Deploy to the project solution. Schema ONLY — the write logic is 050.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke Dataverse schema engineer. Fluent in the `dataverse-create-schema` skill (Web API + PowerShell), junction/intersection modeling, typed-lookup vs polymorphic-lookup trade-offs, the ADR-034 `(personId, personIdType)` tuple intent, and option-set integer conventions. You create exactly the 6-field junction FR-08 locks — nothing more — and you align to ADR-034's intent via two typed lookups.
  </role>

  <goal>
    `sprk_communicationparticipant` exists in the project solution as a message-grain junction with exactly: a required `sprk_communication` Lookup, nullable `sprk_systemuser` + `sprk_contact` Lookups (exactly-one-set is a write invariant), an `sprk_role` Choice {From,To,Cc,Bcc} with the planned integers, `sprk_addresstext` Text, `sprk_isresolved` Boolean, and the primary `sprk_name` Text. A row can be created for a resolved person (one person lookup set, `isresolved=true`) and for an unresolved external address (both person lookups null, `addresstext` set, `isresolved=false`). Tasks 050 (participant-index write) and 051 (`participant=` facet join) can build against real schema; the DataGrid can auto-derive a person chip from the typed lookups.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Person filtering is impossible today: `sprk_from/to/cc` are `;`-separated TEXT, `ThreadMembershipDerivationService` answers record→people (not person→communications), and `ParticipantCorrelationRung` resolves email→contact at capture time but persists nothing queryable (`notes/r2-resource-investigation.md` §5). The junction is the queryable person→communications structure that powers `participant=` (FR-02) with role precision and keeps external parties filterable + back-fillable.

      §11 Component Justification (a NEW entity is introduced — spec §New-Components supplies the concrete cost): (1) **Existing overlap** — none queryable; `sprk_from/to/cc` are `;`-joined TEXT and `ThreadMembershipDerivationService` is record→people, not person→comms (task 001 grep/MCP-confirms no junction exists). (2) **Extension instead** — no existing structure can be extended into a queryable person→communications index; a text-LIKE person filter over the `;`-joined fields gives wrong results with no role precision and can't surface external parties — rejected. (3) **Concrete cost-of-doing-nothing** — without the junction the `participant=` filter is impossible, the person filter degrades to text-LIKE (wrong results, no role precision), and external parties are invisible (spec §New-Components row). Named contract failures (FR-08 acceptance), not "future flexibility."

      ADR-034 tension (spec §ADR Tensions, owner-approved 2026-07-18, path C comply-with-intent): ADR-034's `(personId, personIdType)` tuple exists to avoid an awkward 6-target polymorphic lookup and to forbid fuzzy text-name matching. This junction has only **2** person targets (systemuser, contact), so it uses **two typed nullable lookups** — honoring ADR-034's intent (typed identity, no text-name matching) while adding FK integrity + DataGrid person-chip auto-derivation the tuple can't. That tension is DOCUMENTED by the sibling ADR (task 004); this task implements the locked schema, it does not re-litigate the decision.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/messaging-communication-app-r2/notes/001-phase0-schema-audit.md (task 001 output — confirms NO junction exists yet + the `sprk_role` integer plan; consume it)</file>
